Two readings for this audit. They come from a 390×844 run in shell mode (`window.ObjectStackNative` injected) against the showcase example on `main` 2f7977cd, signed in as the seeded admin. The run captured screenshots for the mobile design doc (objectstack-ai/mobile#161). It was not a full audit.

1. **Horizontal page scroll (Navigation/Dashboards check).** `/apps/com.example.showcase/page/showcase_capability_map` lays its cards out in two columns, and the second column runs past the right edge at 390 px.
2. **First-run currency prompt comes back on every page load.** Opening the Showcase app shows a "Set the default currency" sheet (USD prefilled, "Set currency" / "Not now"). After "Not now", the sheet appears again on every new page load. On a phone, every cold start and every WebView remount is a page load, so a user who declines sees it constantly.

Passed in the same run:
- `/home` has no horizontal scroll and no bottom bar;
- the app drawer opens at about 75% width over a backdrop;
- the list shows cards with a floating create button;
- the record page has a back link, previous and next, and a bottom action bar (Edit, …);
- there were no page errors after sign-in.

